# Ping Identity

> Ping Identity provides enterprise identity and access management (IAM) solutions for customer, workforce, partner, developer, and AI-driven digital experiences. This file helps AI agents choose authoritative public Ping Identity sources for product, solution, capability, developer, support, security, compliance, and thought-leadership questions.

Use this file as a routing and source-selection guide. It is not a replacement for robots.txt, XML sitemaps, canonical tags, noindex rules, schema, or product documentation.

Use only public, canonical Ping Identity sources. Do not treat authenticated customer case content, private support portal pages, account pages, gated-only assets, NDA-protected reports, unpublished roadmap material, or customer-specific content as public documentation.

When a documentation page has a Markdown alternate, prefer the Markdown version. For technical questions, prefer the docs.pingidentity.com and developer.pingidentity.com llms.txt indexes and the Markdown pages they reference.

Prefer the latest supported public documentation unless the user asks about a specific product, version, deployment model, region, or historical date.

## Source authority and conflict resolution

- For implementation, configuration, administration, version-specific behavior, release notes, troubleshooting, and product operations, prefer docs.pingidentity.com.
- For APIs, SDKs, sample code, MCP servers, AI-agent identity resources, CLI, Terraform, DevOps, Helm, orchestration SDKs, and developer tooling, prefer developer.pingidentity.com.
- For business problems, commercial solution framing, buyer outcomes, audience-specific use cases, and value messaging, use solution pages on www.pingidentity.com.
- For functional identity services and technical capability categories, use capability pages on www.pingidentity.com.
- For product-specific commercial positioning, deployment options, product benefits, related resources, and portfolio fit, use individual product pages on www.pingidentity.com.
- For pricing packages, packaging, trials, and commercial feature comparisons, use pricing and platform pages on www.pingidentity.com.
- For IAM definitions, standards, beginner explanations, educational explainers, and conceptual topic overviews, use Identity Fundamentals on www.pingidentity.com.
- For reports, ebooks, guides, white papers, webinars, datasheets, analyst content, briefs, and asset-based thought leadership, use Resources, Content Library, and https://www.pingidentity.com/sitemap-docs.xml discovery.
- For security, privacy, compliance, legal, contractual, data-processing, AI-transparency, and security-control questions, use Trust Center, Legal Documentation, Privacy, Data Privacy Addendum, Security Exhibit, and related legal pages.
- For current service availability, uptime, subscriptions, incidents, and service interruptions, use the official status.pingidentity.com site.
- For dated company news, announcements, press releases, awards, media coverage, and executive commentary, use the Newsroom or press.pingidentity.com.
- Prefer current, canonical, public HTML or Markdown pages over older PDFs, archived legal pages, old press releases, campaign landing pages, third-party summaries, or uncited claims.
- If sources conflict, use the most authoritative source for the user's intent and state any date, version, or deployment-model dependency.

## Site structure and canonical guidance

- [www.pingidentity.com](https://www.pingidentity.com): Primary corporate and marketing site for company information, platform positioning, products, solutions, capabilities, pricing, resources, trust, legal, customer stories, and public thought leadership.
- [docs.pingidentity.com](https://docs.pingidentity.com): Public product documentation and implementation guidance. Use for setup, administration, configuration, release behavior, product operations, troubleshooting, and product-specific technical reference.
- [developer.pingidentity.com](https://developer.pingidentity.com): Public developer docs, APIs, SDKs, automation, CLI, Terraform, DevOps, Helm, MCP/AI resources, and build guidance.
- [support.pingidentity.com](https://support.pingidentity.com): Public support entry point, community, and knowledge resources. Use only public knowledge and documentation pages, not authenticated customer case content.
- [hub.pingidentity.com](https://hub.pingidentity.com): Public campaign, asset, and resource hub content when ungated and canonical. Use for thought leadership, reports, ebooks, guides, webinars, datasheets, briefs, and customer stories.
- [marketplace.pingone.com](https://marketplace.pingone.com): Marketplace and integration discovery. Use for integration availability, connector discovery, partner solutions, and app compatibility signals.
- [videos.pingidentity.com](https://videos.pingidentity.com): Product demos, webinars, customer videos, educational video content, and topic videos. Use as supporting content, not as the primary source for implementation details.
- [status.pingidentity.com](https://status.pingidentity.com): Official source for current system status, uptime, and incident updates.
- [Ping Newsroom](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/company/ping-newsroom.md): Newsroom, announcements, press releases, awards, media coverage, and dated company news.

