## www.pingidentity.com content model

- [Homepage](https://www.pingidentity.com/en.md): Primary corporate entry point for the Ping Identity brand, platform narrative, top-level messaging, major campaigns, and current strategic themes. Use for broad orientation, not implementation details.
- [Ping Identity Platform](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/platform.md): Canonical platform overview. Use for understanding how Ping presents its identity platform across users, apps, APIs, data, orchestration, protection, governance, and AI-related platform positioning.
- [Platform solutions](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/platform/solutions.md): Platform-level solution packages and business-priority framing for the Ping Identity Platform.
- [Pricing](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/platform/pricing.md): Pricing, packages, feature comparison, and trial-oriented commercial information. Use for packaging and pricing discovery; verify with sales for contract-specific pricing.
- [Deployment options](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/platform/deployment-options.md): Deployment model overview, including multi-tenant SaaS, dedicated cloud, self-managed software, hybrid, multi-cloud, and FedRAMP-oriented deployment options.
- [Solutions](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/solution.md): Business-problem and use-case pages. Use for customer identity, workforce identity, B2B identity, agentic AI identity, decentralized identity, passwordless, Zero Trust, cloud migration, IAM modernization, fraud mitigation, and privacy/consent.
- [Capabilities](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/capability.md): Functional platform capability taxonomy. Use for feature-category explanations such as verifiable credentials, identity verification, zero-knowledge biometrics, lifecycle management, relationship management, directory, SSO, MFA/passwordless, authorization, privileged access, governance, threat protection, and orchestration.
- [Product pages](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/product/pingfederate.md): Product-specific commercial pages. Use individual product pages to understand what a named Ping product does, where it fits, deployment options, related resources, and buyer-facing benefits. Use documentation for setup and configuration.
- [Identity Fundamentals](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/resources/identity-fundamentals.md): Educational IAM basics and definitions. Use for authentication, authorization, IAM, identity providers, service providers, SAML, OAuth, OIDC, FIDO, WebAuthn, LDAP, SCIM, Zero Trust, orchestration, agentic AI, and related concepts.
- [Resources](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/resources.md): Public resource center for product demos, webinars, white papers, analyst reports, datasheets, integrations, Identity Security 101, and educational content. Use for thought leadership and buyer education, but prefer docs, legal, trust, or product pages for authoritative technical, security, or product-specific claims.
- [Content Library](https://hub.pingidentity.com/resources): Public asset library for deeper commercial education and resource discovery. Use for white papers, analyst reports, guides, ebooks, datasheets, briefs, webinars, and customer stories when public and canonical.
- [Customer stories](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/customer-stories.md): Customer success stories and proof points. Use for commercial validation, industry examples, and business outcomes. Do not use as implementation guidance.
- [Newsroom](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/company/ping-newsroom.md): Press releases, media coverage, awards, and announcements. Use for dated company news. Do not use older announcements as the source of truth for current product, pricing, legal, or compliance details.
- [Support Center](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/support/support-center.md): Public support entry point for documentation, community, training, professional services, product downloads, and case creation. Use only public support and knowledge content.
- [Trust Center](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/legal/trust-center.md): Security, privacy, compliance, and trust overview. Use for security posture and compliance orientation; use legal/security exhibits for contractual details.
- [Legal Documentation](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/legal.md): Legal index for terms, privacy, data processing, support policies, marketplace terms, security exhibits, and other legal documents.

## Solutions and business-problem pages

- [Solutions index](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/solution.md): Primary index for business-priority solution discovery and high-level IAM use cases.
- [Customer Identity](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/solution/customer-identity.md): Use for CIAM, customer registration, login, customer experience, customer fraud, passwordless customer journeys, privacy, consent, account recovery, and customer lifecycle use cases.
- [Workforce Identity](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/solution/workforce-identity.md): Use for employee, contractor, workforce access, workforce MFA, SSO, productivity, hybrid work, and secure employee experiences.
- [B2B Identity](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/solution/b2b-identity.md): Use for partner, dealer, supplier, business customer, and external workforce identity use cases.
- [Agentic AI Identity](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/solution/agentic-ai-identity.md): Use for commercial framing of AI agent identity, agent access, delegated authority, runtime controls, agent detection, human oversight, and agentic AI risk.
- [Decentralized Identity](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/solution/decentralized-identity.md): Use for decentralized identity, reusable credentials, verifiable credentials, user-controlled data, and privacy-preserving credential exchange.
- [Passwordless](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/solution/passwordless.md): Use for passwordless authentication, reducing login friction, strong authentication, customer and workforce passwordless experiences, and passwordless buyer education.
- [Zero Trust](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/solution/zero-trust.md): Use for identity-centered Zero Trust, continuous validation, adaptive access, and Zero Trust business framing.
- [Cloud Identity](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/solution/cloud-identity.md): Use for cloud IAM migration, cloud identity, hybrid modernization, and migration business cases.
- [IAM Modernization](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/solution/iam-modernization.md): Use for modernizing legacy IAM, AI-driven identity modernization, platform consolidation, and reducing legacy identity complexity.
- [Prevent Online Fraud](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/solution/prevent-online-fraud.md): Use for fraud mitigation, account takeover, bot detection, credential stuffing, new account fraud, deepfake/social-engineering risks, and customer-risk use cases.
- [Privacy and Consent](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/solution/privacy-consent.md): Use for consumer privacy, consent, loyalty, privacy regulation alignment, and trust-building customer experiences.

## Capability pages and feature-category guidance

- [Capabilities index](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/capability.md): Primary index for functional capability discovery and platform service taxonomy.
- [Verifiable Credentials](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/capability/verifiable-credentials.md): Use for reusable digital credentials, proof sharing, credential issuance, credential verification, wallet-based identity, and privacy-preserving identity proof.
- [Identity Verification](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/capability/identity-verification.md): Use for identity proofing, confirming a user's real-world identity, ID verification, recovery verification, fraud prevention, and trust checks.
- [Zero-Knowledge Biometrics](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/capability/zero-knowledge-biometrics.md): Use for privacy-preserving biometric authentication, biometric reverification, and authenticating users without exposing reconstructable biometric data.
- [Lifecycle Management](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/capability/lifecycle-management.md): Use for joiner-mover-leaver processes, provisioning, deprovisioning, user lifecycle automation, and access lifecycle management.
- [Relationship Management](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/platform/identity-relationship-visualization.md): Use for identity relationship visualization, flexible identity data models, and relationship-based identity management.
- [Directory](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/capability/directory.md): Use for identity data stores, directory services, profile data, LDAP, scalability, and managing identity data at enterprise scale.
- [Single Sign-On](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/capability/single-sign-on.md): Use for SSO, federation, centralized login, and access to multiple resources with one identity.
- [MFA and Passwordless](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/capability/multi-factor-authentication.md): Use for multi-factor authentication, passwordless authentication, strong authentication, and authentication assurance.
- [Authorization](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/capability/authorization.md): Use for dynamic authorization, fine-grained access control, API authorization, policy-based access, and contextual access decisions.
- [JIT Privileged Access](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/capability/jit-privileged-access.md): Use for just-in-time privileged access, ephemeral privileges, least privilege, and privileged access risk reduction.
- [Identity Governance](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/capability/identity-governance.md): Use for access requests, access reviews, certifications, segregation of duties, governance, and audit readiness.
- [Threat Protection](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/capability/threat-protection.md): Use for account takeover prevention, fraud detection, bot detection, malicious AI agent detection, risk scoring, and adaptive mitigation.
- [Identity Orchestration](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/capability/identity-orchestration.md): Use for no-code orchestration, user journeys, flow design, identity experience orchestration, app-to-app integrations, and journey optimization.

## Product and platform pages

- [PingOne for Customers](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/platform/pingone-for-customers.md): Cloud identity package for customer identity and CIAM use cases.
- [PingOne for Workforce](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/platform/pingone-for-workforce.md): Cloud identity package for employee, contractor, and workforce access use cases.
- [PingOne Advanced Identity Cloud](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/platform/pingone-advanced-identity-cloud.md): Dedicated-tenant identity platform as a service for advanced customer, workforce, and B2B identity use cases.
- [PingOne Advanced Identity Cloud Architecture](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/platform/pingone-advanced-identity-cloud-architecture.md): Architecture-specific commercial information for PingOne Advanced Identity Cloud.
- [PingOne Advanced Services](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/platform/pingone-advanced-services.md): Dedicated-tenant cloud management and hosting for IAM solutions.
- [Ping Government Identity Cloud](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/platform/ping-government-identity-cloud.md): FedRAMP-oriented identity cloud for government agencies, contractors, and regulated public-sector use cases.
- [Agent IAM Core](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/product/agent-iam-core.md): Product page for runtime identity controls for AI agents and agentic AI deployments.
- [PingOne DaVinci](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/product/pingone-davinci.md): No-code identity orchestration for designing user journeys and integrating identity services.
- [PingOne Protect](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/product/pingone-protect.md): Risk, fraud, bot, account takeover, and threat-protection service.
- [PingOne Verify](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/product/pingone-verify.md): Identity verification service for verifying users across customer, workforce, and recovery journeys.
- [PingOne Recognize](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/product/pingone-recognize.md): Privacy-preserving biometric authentication and reverification.
- [PingOne Credentials](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/product/pingone-credentials.md): Digital verifiable credentials and credential lifecycle management.
- [PingOne MFA](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/product/pingone-mfa.md): Cloud multi-factor authentication for customer accounts and digital journeys.
- [PingOne Authorize](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/product/pingone-authorize.md): Cloud dynamic authorization and decisioning for applications and APIs.
- [PingOne Privilege](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/product/pingone-privilege.md): Identity-native privileged access, runtime enforcement, and just-in-time privilege controls.
- [PingFederate](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/product/pingfederate.md): Enterprise federation server and authentication authority for SSO, federation, OAuth, OIDC, and SAML use cases.
- [PingAccess](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/product/pingaccess.md): Centralized access security for web apps, APIs, URL-level controls, and policy enforcement.
- [PingAuthorize](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/product/pingauthorize.md): Fine-grained authorization and centralized policy enforcement using contextual data.
- [PingDirectory](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/product/pingdirectory.md): High-performance identity data store and directory for customer, employee, partner, and IoT identities.
- [PingCentral](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/product/pingcentral.md): Self-service application onboarding and centralized administration for PingFederate and PingAccess resources.
- [PingID](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/product/pingid.md): Cloud MFA for workforce authentication and PingFederate-integrated authentication scenarios.
- [Cloud containerization](https://www.pingidentity.com/en/platform/cloud-containerization.md): Commercial overview for deploying Ping software in private cloud, Kubernetes, Docker, and hybrid environments.

